Z||000000||Fierokid87||06-03-2001||01:07 AM||||Hey guys I have a borla exuast (not for sale) and was wondering if anyone has any experience with the system?  And how does it sound and if anyone has sound files they might like to share.  Thanks<P>Scott||||reg||3
Z||000001||stevemasleid||06-03-2001||03:49 AM||||I have the Borla on my 86 GT. Meinike charged me one hundred to install it. It kida sounds like a late 90's Z28, I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||06-03-2001||10:41 AM||||Hey, Fierokid, let me know how you make out with that. I was thinking about getting one of those myself. But first I need to find a header for my 4cyl.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierokid87||06-03-2001||10:49 AM||||Yep I will let you know how I make out on this.  But I wont know how it sounds till like November when my V-6 Conversion is done.<P>Scott<P>AIM: Fieorkid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P>website: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero/</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||88formula||06-03-2001||11:30 AM||||It sounds like the original exhaust system only deeper and a little throaty. It's not overly loud and that is what I like about it. It’s just right for sound. It sounds real mean.<P>Best thing to do is go to a fiero show in your area and listen to a car that has a Borla exhaust. You'll also notice improved gas mileage and you will gain a few ponies too.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DecadenceR||06-03-2001||01:34 PM||||Okay, as long as it sounds good. i don't want to sound like all the rice burners. <BR>I have to replace my exhaust soon anyway, and since Borla is one of the bst, if not the best, names in aftermarket, I figured what the hell....||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTZ34||06-03-2001||04:20 PM||||Fierokid,  Yes the Borla is an improvement over the stock system.  As 88formula said, it is deeper but not loud.  Mine has slight resonance @ 2k but it is very subtle.  I have a high flow cat on it so it may be somewhat louder if you decide to run w/o the cat.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DecadenceR||06-03-2001||10:37 PM||||hey 87GTZ, did you put on a header with that too? because that's what i have planned. Header into a high flow cat with the Borla ezhaust.<BR>Wish I had the money to do it today, my mouth is watering already.. LOL||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GTZ34||06-04-2001||09:54 AM||||No,  This is on my stocker.  The only thing I did was to weld and clean out the exhaust ports.  Putting headers on that one would make it run worse (less torque).  Alex4mula has headers, no cat and the Borla on his 3.4 and it is slightly louder than mine.  Of course my exhaust has about 50 mi on it so it may 'loosen' up a bit.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||06-04-2001||10:45 AM||||Cool Ron! Good to hear yours in now. <BR>Borlas sound good. Not too loud. Just right. As 87GTZ said, mine is with headers, no cat in a 3.4. One club member has a Flowmaster with a 2.8 and the FM is louder than mine. Another comparison I use to have no cat, no muffler and resonator tips. That was way loud. Go with the Borla. You won't be dissapointed.||||reg||1
